course: dictionary
lesson: 3537
title: Fed: food, feeding and fed up
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Fed» is the past form of «feed», which means to give food to a person or an animal. It can also describe a person who has had enough to eat, as in «well-fed».
explain: The sentences show the meaning. «Even well-fed pet cats still hunt» tells you the cats have had plenty to eat, and they still hunt anyway. «Children stay warm and fed» means they have food and are looked after.
explain: Use the swap test. In «keeping everyone safe and fed», replace fed with «had food». It still makes sense, so you have found the meaning.
fact: «Fed» is the past form of «feed»: feed, feeds, fed, feeding.
fact: «Well fed» means having had plenty to eat.
fact: «Fed up» is informal and means bored, annoyed or unhappy with something that has gone on too long.
fact: «Feed» can also mean giving something needed into a machine, like feeding paper into a printer.
fact: «Fed on» means ate as food: the owl fed on mice.
exercise: «Cats are ambush hunters, and even well-fed pet cats still hunt.» What does well-fed mean here? | Lost and hungry | *Having had plenty to eat | Tired of waiting | Very fast and quick
exercise: Mum says, «I fed the cat before school.» What did Mum do? | *Gave food to the cat | Gave the cat a bath | Put the cat in a box | Taught the cat to hunt
exercise: Tom says, «I am fed up with waiting for the bus.» What does fed up mean? | Full of food | Very happy and excited | Ready to run fast | *Bored and annoyed
test: In the science book, «the owl fed on mice». What does fed on mean here? | Hid from mice | Chased mice away | *Ate mice as food | Gave mice to the owl in a box
test: «The paper was fed into the printer.» What does fed mean here? | Ate food | *Gave something needed into a machine | Ran away quickly | Was bored and annoyed
exam: In «help schemes exist so children stay warm and fed», what does fed mean? | *Having food to eat | Sent into a machine | Chased and caught | Bored and annoyed with waiting
